                            "U.S. officials held up equipment export licenses for SK hynix\u0027s Dalian, China fab (reported Nov 3, 2026), complicating Solidigm\u0027s $45 billion-plus New York expansion.",
                            "Q3 net profit dropped to KRW 39.78 trillion on FX and valuation losses, while a U.S. judge refused to dismiss a DRAM price-fixing lawsuit on Nov 14, 2026."
                        ],
               "fundamental":  "Fundamentally, SK hynix remains at the center of AI data-center infrastructure as NVIDIA\u0027s core High Bandwidth Memory (HBM) partner for Blackwell and next-generation Vera Rubin platforms. On Oct 28, 2026, Q3 revenue crossed KRW 100 trillion for the first time at KRW 104.62 trillion (+328% YoY, +32% QoQ), while operating profit jumped 632% YoY to KRW 83.33 trillion (79.7% margin) across HBM4, server DDR5, and 321-layer enterprise SSDs. Management expects HBM4 to overtake HBM3E in Q4 2026 as the M15X fab ramps, with over half of 2027–2028 capacity committed under long-term agreements. Still, significant 2027 CapEx expansion for the Yongin cluster, Samsung\u0027s HBM4 catch-up, and paused Solidigm IPO plans make margin durability the central debate.",
               "headline":  "Record Q3 Profits Collide With Peak-Cycle Fears and Rising HBM4 Rivalry",
               "news":  [
                            "Oct 23 \u0026 Oct 28, 2026: SK hynix discontinued its U.S. IPO review for NAND subsidiary Solidigm, citing unfavorable capital market conditions.",
