                            "Oct 28, 2026: Q3 2026 revenue surged 328% YoY to KRW 104.62 trillion with KRW 83.33 trillion in operating profit (79.7% margin), while management guided HBM4 to surpass HBM3E in Q4 2026.",
                            "Nov 3, 2026: Reuters reported U.S. officials held up export licenses for American chipmaking tools destined for SK hynix\u0027s Dalian, China fab, snagging Solidigm\u0027s $45 billion-plus New York plant plans.",
                            "Nov 14 \u0026 Nov 16, 2026: A U.S. judge denied SK hynix, Samsung, and Micron\u0027s motion to dismiss a DRAM price-fixing class-action suit, two days before SK hynix unveiled a KRW 1.4 trillion ($1.05 billion) five-year domestic supplier support fund.",
                            "Nov 20, 2026: SK hynix filed to convert JPY 129 billion ($810 million) of bonds (closing Dec 4) into a 14.1% indirect stake in Kioxia, becoming the Japanese NAND maker\u0027s largest indirect shareholder."
                        ],
               "opportunity":  "If AI accelerator demand stays durable through NVIDIA\u0027s Vera Rubin transition, SK hynix\u0027s multi-year LTA coverage (over 50% of 2027–2028 capacity) and Q4 2026 HBM4 crossover provide unusually strong revenue visibility compared with prior memory cycles. Near-term technical stabilization near the KRW 984,016 lower Bollinger Band could also be supported by roughly KRW 13.4 trillion ($9.9 billion) in remaining share buybacks once South Korea eases daily buyback limits on Nov 24, 2026, alongside promised special dividends from Kioxia investment gains.",
               "opportunityCheck":  "The page\u0027s strong marks for AI revenue exposure, market growth, and bottleneck pricing power remain justified by Q3\u0027s KRW 104.62 trillion revenue, 79.7% operating margin, HBM4 crossover, and multi-year capacity lock-in. However, I would trim the market-position score slightly: Bernstein\u0027s Oct 26 analysis indicates Samsung has rapidly closed the HBM revenue gap during the HBM4 ramp, shifting SK hynix from undisputed dominance toward a tight duopoly. Conversely, optionality deserves a modest lift as SK hynix converts Kioxia bonds into a 14.1% indirect NAND stake and expands CXL and memory-pooling solutions.",
