               "summary":  "SK hynix (KRX:000660) delivered historic Q3 2026 results on Oct 28—KRW 104.62 trillion in revenue and KRW 83.33 trillion in operating profit (79.7% margin)—as HBM4 entered full mass production. Yet shares have fallen 63.7% from their KRW 2,987,000 52-week high to KRW 1,083,000 on Nov 23 amid AI-monetization jitters, peak-margin fears, and heavy KOSPI foreign outflows. An Oct 26 Bernstein estimate suggesting Samsung rivaled or topped SK hynix in Q3 HBM revenue, alongside U.S. export-license delays in Dalian (Nov 3), puts the long-term moat thesis on watch.",
               "technical":  "As of Nov 23, 2026, SK hynix trades at KRW 1,083,000 (-2.7% on the day) in a firmly bearish downtrend across 484 trading days of history. Price sits more than 22% below all three exponential moving averages (EMAs, which smooth price trends): EMA 50 at KRW 1,403,220, EMA 200 at KRW 1,418,374, and EMA 100 at KRW 1,512,307. Notably, EMA 50 has crossed beneath EMA 200—a classic bearish \"death cross.\" Momentum confirms weakness: MACD (a trend-momentum gauge) stands at -96,873 below its -93,858 signal line with a negative -3,015 histogram, while RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) sits at 36.41, weak but not yet oversold. Within the Bollinger Bands (a 20-day volatility channel), price lies well under the KRW 1,263,500 middle line (initial resistance) and 9.1% above the KRW 984,016 lower band (near-term support), sitting in the bottom quarter of its KRW 501,000–2,987,000 52-week range (-63.7% from the peak). Daily volume of 3.11 million shares ran 19% below the 3.84 million 20-day average, showing muted panic selling on the latest dip."
